title: The Proletarian Hundreds
subtitle: Workers' defence units, a hundred men each. Who arms them, and how openly?
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: rf_mass
view-if: rf_hundreds_timer <= 0 and party_banned = 0 and year = 1923
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rf_hundreds_timer = 3

= The Proletarian Hundreds

Since 1922 the party has organised Proletarian Hundreds: workers' units for defending meetings and factories against the right-wing leagues. In Saxony and Thuringia they are tolerated, even legal. Elsewhere the police break them up.

- @open
- @secret

@open
title: Build them openly, together with <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> workers.
subtitle: Pleases the <span class="f-right">Right</span>. Improves relations with the <span class="p-spd">SPD</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 3});
Q.readiness += 5;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.repression += 3;
!}

Joint units of Communist and Social Democratic workers drill in Saxon factory yards. They have few weapons but real numbers.

@secret
title: Arm them in secret through the party's military apparatus.
subtitle: Much more readiness. Pleases the <span class="f-left">Left</span> and <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span>. Costs 1 fund; draws the police.
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Weapons cost money the party does not have.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {left: 3, ultra: 2, right: -2});
Q.funds -= 1;
Q.readiness += 8;
Q.repression += 6;
!}

The party's military apparatus buys rifles where it can and hides them in allotment sheds. There are never as many as the reports to Moscow claim.
